      "node_id": "kg_doc_3",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Title: Brown State Fishing Lake. Brown State Fishing Lake (sometimes also known as Brown State Fishing Lake And Wildlife Area) is a protected area in Brown County, Kansas in the United States. The lake is 62 acres (0.25 km²) in area and up to 13 feet (4 m) deep. The area was formerly known as Brown County State Park, and is 8 miles (13 km) east of Hiawatha, Kansas.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
